\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Stephen Laine}{
 [00:22:45\u8211\'9600:23:36]\line Yeah. And so, so I go over there, pick him up from his life skills school, come back home. And I'm like, you know, I'm, I'm doing my old methods of calming him down, making sure he doesn't escalate or anything. And at this point, he seems like he's not escalating at all. Everything seems to be okay.\line And I'm like, you know what, I'm gonna try and go\u8212\'97 I tell my mom, she's gonna watch him. I'm also like, I'm gonna try and go to work. I think he's fine now. You know, I think it was just You know, he doesn't seem elevated or anything. And so I go to work.\line Not even 5 to 10 minutes later, I get a phone call. Matthew ran away again. And so we're looking\u8212\'97 so I drive back home and I pull into my driveway. Here's Matthew sprinting back home carrying a bunch of DVDs.\line And so\u8212\'97\line And I want to let you know where I live. It's about 5 to 6 houses away from a very busy road.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:23:43\u8211\'9600:23:47]\line Oh, sure. Right, right. So yeah, it's terrifying.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Stephen Laine}{
 [00:23:47\u8211\'9600:23:48]\line It's terrifying.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:23:48\u8211\'9600:23:49]\line Yeah.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Stephen Laine}{
 [00:23:49\u8211\'9600:24:36]\line So anyways, I've got\u8212\'97 I have Matthew wear this little lanyard. It says, I have autism, with his name on it and my phone number if he was ever to go missing. So I get a phone call from this guy. He says to me, are you Steven? Are you Matthew Lane's dad?\line I'm like, yes, I am. Who is this? He's like, well, he just tried\u8212\'97 he just went into my house. And he took a bunch of movies. And I'm like, oh, in order to get in, I said, where do you live?\line And he lives on the other side of this very busy road. And Matthew's got\u8212\'97 and Matthew doesn't have a\u8212\'97 Matthew doesn't do really well crossing busy intersections. So I'm thinking to myself, he could have easily gotten hit by a car.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Stephen Laine}{
 [00:24:37\u8211\'9600:25:22]\line So I'm like, okay, I'm gonna take the DVD. I said, so he's\u8212\'97 my son's elevated. He's trying to run away again. And so I'm like, I'm calling into work. I'm not going into work after this.\line You know, he's just too worked up. So I take him. So I\u8212\'97 after he did calm down, I brought the DVDs back. I managed to get ahold of his psychiatrist. And so I got him into the next day to see his doctor.\line I told her everything that's been going on. We do a new regimen of meds with him and see if that works. And at this point, I'm like, well, this is becoming a big issue now with him. I'm ordering AngelSense GPS on him. And so I got overnighted.\line I'm like, this, we got to do this.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:25:22\u8211\'9600:25:25]\line Yeah, yeah. You want to be able to see where he is.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Stephen Laine}{
 [00:25:25\u8211\'9600:26:04]\line Yeah. Yep. So, um, so we ordered\u8212\'97 I ordered that. And so Again, week goes by, he's doing okay, no issues really. And so, and I end up taking, you know, some time off of work just to observe him on his new bed to see how he was doing. And so third time I'm like, okay, well, I'm gonna\u8212\'97 so third time that happened was, okay, I think he's all right. And so it was on Sunday, my\u8212\'97 I was gonna go to my best friend's house on Sunday afternoon. And my best friend, he lives right around the block from me. And we've been lifelong friends. We've known each other for almost 40 years.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:26:04\u8211\'9600:26:06]\line Oh, wow. That's great. Great.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Stephen Laine}{
 [00:26:06\u8211\'9600:26:31]\line Yeah, we're practically like brothers. So I go over there. And then guess what happens? I look at my phone. Matthew left my house. And so I'm like, oh my God. So he's crossed. So I'm following the GPS. He's crossing this very busy road over and over again. And I'm like, oh my God, he's got to get killed. He's got to get killed.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:26:31\u8211\'9600:26:34]\line Your heart must have been racing. I mean, it was.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Stephen Laine}{
 [00:26:34\u8211\'9600:27:41]\line It was. I mean, multiple times he's crossing this very busy road with a speed limit of 35 miles an hour. There's traffic at all times. And I'm like, oh my God, he's just got to get himself killed. I'm going to be going to his funeral.\line That's exactly what I'm thinking. And so I find him, Thankfully, I had the GPS on him. I find him in a store. And it's a store that has like video games, DVDs, toys, you know, the whole nine yards. And so he's like, he's like got a whole rack.\line He's got a whole thing of them. Like, he's got like at least about $200 worth of merchandise in his hands. I'm like, hey, Matthew, we gotta put these back. He goes, no, I'm gonna take them. I'm gonna take them.\line So no, we gotta put these back. And so he's just trying to ransack through the store with me in there with him. And so I called the police. I'm like, I can't, you know, he's still elevated now. He's gonna have to go back to the ER. And so I called the police.\line And I don't know what schools are like over in your area, but in our area, we're in Michigan, a lot of the schools have what we call a police resource officer.\line Mm-hmm.\line And so we have that here in Michigan where there's a cop on the grounds of the school. And I know him, he's really a nice guy, great guy. So anyways, guess who shows up? Matthew's resource officer that he knew from high school.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:27:57\u8211\'9600:27:59]\line Oh, that's helpful, right?}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Stephen Laine}{
 [00:27:59\u8211\'9600:28:15]\line Yeah, it was very helpful. Yeah. I mean, I already knew the police in my department and where I live, they're really good with Matthew. And it was kind of funny because it's some of the same police officers that showed up at the last incident. They kind of knew what they were dealing with.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:28:15\u8211\'9600:28:21]\line So yeah, yeah. I mean, that's good, right? Like, yeah, it's, it's, I mean, everyone's kind of familiar with the situation.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Stephen Laine}{
 [00:28:21\u8211\'9600:29:21]\line Exactly. Exactly. So anyways, you know, we get them, you know, the police officers are, you know, de-escalating, you know, de-escalating the situation with them. So anyways, officers get in there, they, you know, get them into the ambulance. And so I'm waiting at the ER, and I know like, this is this This is getting really bad at this point.\line And so we wait in the ER and we're just waiting. And the psychiatrist shows up and I tell him what's going on. And he says, we're probably going to have to look at inpatient psychiatric for him. And I'm like, well, okay. And in Michigan, there isn't a whole lot of psychiatric hospitals.\line There really isn't. And so You're pretty much waiting until a bed opens up and you just can't just pick whichever one you want to go to. You just got to wait until there's an opening. And so I'm like, well, I'm just going to stay here at the ER with my son until there's an opening. If I got to wait here a week, I'll wait here a week.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Announcer}{
 [00:29:21\u8211\'9600:29:22]\line Mm-hmm.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Stephen Laine}{
 [00:29:22\u8211\'9600:29:46]\line And it did come to that. The next day, we did find him a bed at a psychiatric hospital. And so they transported him over there. And they dropped him off at nighttime and I'm coming back home and my mind's just racing. I felt like I just abandoned my son.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:29:46\u8211\'9600:29:47]\line Right. That'd be so hard.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Stephen Laine}{
 [00:29:47\u8211\'9600:30:10]\line It was. It was. And so I returned and so I'm like, this is just so much. I don't know what the future's going to happen. I don't know how they're going to rule this. I don't know if If he's going to be returning back home or if he's going to be, you know, in some kind of residential facility. I don't know what's going on.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:30:10\u8211\'9600:30:11]\line Right. Right.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Stephen Laine}{
 [00:30:11\u8211\'9600:30:13]\line A million thoughts are running through my head at this point.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:30:13\u8211\'9600:31:00]\line Well, I'm curious, Steve, what kinds of things were they telling you in terms of the psychiatric aspect, in terms of having him admitted to a psychiatric ward? Because I think that's something that You know, again, people would be interested in it. It's, it's, you know, we've talked a lot about how behaviors, quote unquote, can be misinterpreted. Impulsive behavior, you know, there's a lot of things that kids like our kids can do that tend to be kind of uniquely autistic, you know, and not necessarily a sign of something underneath it from a psychiatric standpoint.\line So I'm kind of curious in terms of what the\u8212\'97 the thinking was there.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Stephen Laine}{
 [00:31:00\u8211\'9600:31:15]\line Well, I'm glad you brought that up because when he was at the ER at the hospital he was at, there was a lot of inaccurate information that was forwarded to the psychiatric hospital. And one of those things that they said was that he was aggressive.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:31:15\u8211\'9600:31:18]\line Well, that's a red flag right there.\line Yeah.\line I mean, that kind of sets the tone for who they're dealing with.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Stephen Laine}{
 [00:31:23\u8211\'9600:31:42]\line Well, think about it like this. All right. You know, you're in a strange environment and they're trying to do a blood draw and, you know, you've got 4 to 6 big security guys holding you down to do a blood draw. Well, any kind of\u8212\'97}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:31:42\u8211\'9600:31:55]\line Exactly right. Anytime you're dealing with restraint, with most\u8212\'97 I mean, again, neurotypical people, I mean, you're going to\u8212\'97 a lot of people are going to respond to that.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Stephen Laine}{
 [00:31:56\u8211\'9600:32:08]\line And when we were in the ER, I mean, there was like all these people coming in there that were just up all hours of the night screaming, and it wasn't a good place for him at all.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:32:08\u8211\'9600:32:26]\line No, no, it's\u8212\'97 no, I mean, for, for someone, I'm sure, again, we had to talk about this, but I would imagine there's sensory issues, right? I mean, yeah, right, like sensory input he's probably very sensitive to. I mean, it's, it's kind of Yes. The worst case scenario.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Stephen Laine}{
 [00:32:26\u8211\'9600:33:39]\line And I said, look here, that's totally inaccurate. He is not aggressive. He's not aggressive at all. He's one of the kindest people that you can meet. Because when he went to a psychiatric hospital, that's exactly what I told him.\line I said, no, that is not accurate information at all. You know, and so, and when he was in a psychiatric hospital, there was a point that, you know, he was calling me every day, you know, And I said, right now, your job is to be in the hospital right now. That's one thing that does help with Matthew and his brother Aiden is like, they tell me they have jobs to do. And that helps them cope, right? Your job is to be in the hospital right now.\line And then, you know, we'll go from there, Matthew. Okay. So I'm talking to him 4 or 5, you know, I'm talking to him every day for about 10, 15 minutes, you know, over the phone. That's great. And then all of a sudden, I'm not hearing from him.\line So I'm upset at this point. They're not considering that he might have some abandonment issues. Again, they're not considering these things. And so I got into pretty much a shouting match with his caseworker over this because I'd say, well, why hasn't he called me in 5 days? What is going on?\line No one has updated me on anything.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:33:39\u8211\'9600:33:44]\line And so Yeah, you're totally in the dark for like\u8212\'97}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Stephen Laine}{
 [00:33:44\u8211\'9600:33:47]\line Yeah, I was totally in the dark about 4 or 5 days.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Stephen Laine}{
 [00:33:48\u8211\'9600:34:18]\line Yeah. So part of that was over\u8212\'97 I mean, I understand part of it was over the weekend. But yeah, so last I heard from him was Thursday, and then I didn't hear\u8212\'97 so I didn't hear back from him at all. I had to call them on like that Tuesday or Wednesday and say, well, what's going on here? He hasn't called me or anything. You know, you're dealing with someone who's autistic, who's got abandonment issues. You know, he probably thinks I abandoned him and left him. You people are not seeing it like that.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:34:18\u8211\'9600:35:11]\line Well, exactly. I was thinking about this as you're telling the story, Steve, in terms of these multiple incidents. And again, I'm, you know, I'm just a dad. I'm not an expert. But it does seem to be the common thread there, right?\line Like in terms of the elopement, tended to happen when you were gone, when you're, you know, when you, you know, you were just, you weren't there for him. There's, you know, there's, there's an obvious attachment, which I'm sure is, you know, is so special on one hand, right? Like there's the bond. I have no doubt that you have, because you cannot not have it again, being in those shoes. But yeah, that's, you know, that may be, you know, one of those situations where, whether he may be going through something that just when dad's gone, that he just flipped a switch as well, it sounds like.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Stephen Laine}{
 [00:35:11\u8211\'9600:36:09]\line Yeah. And so they kept me in the dark, you know, and then, you know, eventually it's like, kind of like when he was in the hospital, it was like, okay, we'll keep him here, stabilize him and give him back to his dad. And so that did happen. And then, you know, I got the paperwork back. And the only thing that was on his paperwork as far as follow-up is follow up with a psychiatrist.\line That was it. It was like, okay, you just kept him there, gave him a new regimen of meds. And right, I don't think there was that much help in that hospital, you know. And, you know, that's really unfortunate. And I know it's not just to the hospital he was at.\line I feel like that's probably a problem throughout the whole United States. You know, when it comes to hospitalization amongst those with disabilities or special needs. I know some people don't like the word disability, so I'll use special needs.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:36:09\u8211\'9600:36:21]\line So yeah, I mean, I think people, you know, again, people know. I mean, yeah, look, a lot, a lot of times you're dealing with, they have disabilities, you know, again, it just, it's just how you define it.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Stephen Laine}{
 [00:36:21\u8211\'9600:36:57]\line Yeah. So when he came home, I put multiple locks throughout every door in my house. Um, I stayed with them for 2 weeks. And so I took a leave of absence from my, from my employer, stayed with them, made sure everything was going smoothly. And then so I've been back to work now for about a week and a half. And there's been no attempts at elopement. And he hasn't asked for DVDs, Blu-rays, or video games. So he hasn't even asked about So far so good. So, so far so good. Yeah. So hopefully we continue on this route.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:36:57\u8211\'9600:37:10]\line And it sounds like from your post, Steve, again, that you've been, I mean, you've been processing a lot obviously, uh, but you've also been spending a lot of time with him talking to him.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:37:12\u8211\'9600:37:45]\line Have you been trying to talk through this, you know, in a way? Because one of the things that, um, I think you had posted again that really struck me was, you know, you're saying like healing doesn't begin the day Someone is discharged, you know, and so you've been dealing with this, the healing from the trauma of being hospitalized to being in a, you know, this foreign environment around different people, all of this. So now you're kind of dealing with this post-event trauma. How are you trying to, how are you processing that? And how are you trying to work with that with Matthew?}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Stephen Laine}{
 [00:37:45\u8211\'9600:38:16]\line Well, right now, probably the first few days were probably the hardest because All he wanted to do was sleep and sleep and sleep. And so I was really concerned at that point. He did manage to get himself out of that. And so he was, at that point, he kept on saying to me, is hospital all done? And I said, yes, Matthew, the hospital is all done. He says, no more hospital. No more hospital.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:38:19\u8211\'9600:38:20]\line Yeah.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Stephen Laine}{
 [00:38:20\u8211\'9600:39:09]\line Matthew will internalize a lot of his emotions, but in his own way, it will come out. Sure. Yeah. I'm just letting him kind of bring it out at his own pace, what he's feeling and all that. As far as healing, I've been just staying there for him as much as I can. Um, now his brother, he, he's actually\u8212\'97 when Matthew went to the hospital, Aiden actually did remarkably well, better than I thought he would do. However, since Matthew's return, his anxiety has actually increased, uh, dramatically, and I feel it is due to he's afraid of another incident happening with his brother. Sure.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:39:09\u8211\'9600:39:11]\line Yeah, because he He witnessed the\u8212\'97}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Stephen Laine}{
 [00:39:11\u8211\'9600:39:22]\line Because he witnessed the one incident that was across the street from my house. He witnessed his brother going into the ambulance and he thought the police were coming to take him away forever.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:39:22\u8211\'9600:39:30]\line Right. Yeah. That's a natural fear to have in terms of\u8212\'97 and it probably was very chaotic and\u8212\'97}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Stephen Laine}{
 [00:39:30\u8211\'9600:39:43]\line Oh yeah. Yeah. And I keep on telling Aiden, you know, the police are not there to take Matthew away. They were there to help. And so that's helping him process his emotions as well.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:39:43\u8211\'9600:40:15]\line And you've said, you know, this is one of the things that resonated because I said in our own case, Stone, who's visiting again\u8212\'97 hi, Stone\u8212\'97 um, you know, has had to deal with his own traumatic incidents, um, and including obviously just in his case being non-speaking for nearly 16 years. And you can only imagine what that can do. But also he has epilepsy. And so he has seizures sometimes, you know, which are scary as hell, as you can imagine.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
