\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:40:16\u8211\'9600:41:00]\line Um, so it was really interesting in our case, you know, coming\u8212\'97 when he began to communicate, it opened up his world and so much. But you talked about internalizing feelings, internalizing trauma. And again, that really struck because we saw that with Stone. And so I realized how traumatized he was just in terms of how he wanted to be even closer to me. So, you know, things, holding hands, just making sure like, you know, it was like a minor elopement.\line I take our dog for a walk. I told you we wake up like uber early and we go for a walk. There's a time that he had left the house. It was like at the school where I take the dog for a walk. And this was like in the middle of winter, barefoot, you know?}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
