David Kaufer}{
 [00:42:48\u8211\'9600:42:49]\line Yeah. Oh yeah.\line Yeah.\line It kept going. I kept thinking like, okay, it's over now. Nope.\line Nope.\line It's not. There's another.\line Yeah.\line So he sat there for a whole 2 and a half hours and he was great. So that was, that's a recent victory that we had with him.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:43:01\u8211\'9600:43:12]\line That's it. And that's a big one. And good, good, good on you, Steve, for taking him and not, not shying away from that kind of a challenge.\line Right.\line I mean, like you said, you didn't just wait the sensory-friendly opportunities are amazing. I'm so glad that we have those now. Like, again, that we've come that far as a society. But it's also nice if you don't have to wait for that or hope for that, right? Like, if you're in a situation like, hey, let's just, let's go see a movie. So that's good. I mean, I think that's really cool.}
