\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:49:03\u8211\'9600:49:42]\line We're here with your tip of the week, strategies and wisdom just for you. Autism parents, we know what you go through. All right, it's time for our autism tip of the week. And, you know, I know you didn't initially come into this, uh, episode with a tip of the week, but I'm wondering if looking back now, Steve, if you, you know, kind of the experience that you had dealing with, you know, a major incident or anything like that. Is there maybe a piece of advice that you learned from this most recent episode that you want to share?}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Stephen Laine}{
 [00:49:42\u8211\'9600:50:18]\line Yeah, it's just that I think what you need to do is surround yourself with a strong support system. You know, and I'm gonna tell you, a lot of people, you know, whether it's online or in my personal life, they really came through. during these past couple months, you know, with these incidents I've had with my oldest son, Matthew. And they've came through in ways I didn't imagine that would happen. So a much\u8212\'97 a great thank you to them. So I think that's what you ultimately need if you're an autism parent, a strong support system behind you.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:50:18\u8211\'9600:50:55]\line You're so right. I mean, it's critical. It's absolutely critical. Um, I can't imagine, like you said, trying to do it without having some level of support system, whether it's family, family and friends in your case, it sounds like, which I'm so happy that you have. So that's a great tip.\line So if you're out there, again, search for that. I mean, you can't\u8212\'97 don't try to do this. Don't try to do this alone. It's, um, you know, no one's Superman, no one's Superwoman, you know, to be able to do it all alone. Okay, the next segment we're gonna have is called Autism Fact or Fiction.\line Get QuickTime ready, and here we go.}
