Stephen Laine}{
 [00:54:51\u8211\'9600:55:13]\line As of right now, I'm doing just a Facebook post right now. Eventually, I'll probably do more. you know, down the road maybe hit other platforms, but the best place for right now is my Facebook, which is Steven, S-T-E-V-E-N, and then my last name, Lane, L-A-I-N-E. It's like the car lane but with the I in the middle.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:55:13\u8211\'9600:55:29]\line With I in it. Yeah. So again, I encourage, uh, listeners to follow Steve or, you know, friend him. I don't know, Steve, how, how, uh, Like, I'm filtering, I'm unfriending people, but you always, you can always follow people on Facebook.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:55:30\u8211\'9600:56:21]\line Yeah. See what they're posting. Okay. The last, the last quick segment we want to have, because we do want to add, you know, I like to end things on a positive note. And that's one of the things, again, I appreciate about your writing and your posts is even as you keep them as real as they are, some, again, raw in certain cases, uh, you always I think find a way to show some level of optimism, some, some kind of hope.\line And I think, you know, in general, we all need hope in this world, this crazy, incredibly weird world right now, but particularly again with the complexities that autism parents face. So, um, we'll go ahead and kick off what we call the Light of the Week. Light on the Spectrum, a moment, person, or story bringing Something good.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Stephen Laine}{
 [00:56:22\u8211\'9600:56:34]\line It feels hopeful, grounded, not performative. Use it for a person, a moment, a breakthrough, a story.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:56:34\u8211\'9600:56:48]\line All right, so it's actually light on the spectrum. One of these weeks I'll get it right. I know my producer Dave is laughing behind the scenes. Okay, but Steve, what, uh, what's a moment over the past few months that And gave you hope?}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Stephen Laine}{
 [00:56:48\u8211\'9600:57:29]\line Well, what gave me hope is all the people that really came through for me and that's been there for me. Like I said, you see a lot of dark things right now in the times we're living in. When I see all these people come through, give me support, especially with the things that have been going on with my oldest son Matthew, it's really putting my faith back into society. And, you know, the people I surround myself with are great people. And if we could do this, you know, who knows what we could do down the road collectively as a whole within the autism community. Yeah.}
